%%%%%%Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/2apcz227
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   On December 18, 2024|pn|hondo717,vs_bbo,aspiring,Rustgi65|
md|1SAJ9763HAQ765DCT7,SQ2HT2DA973CKJ864,ST54H4DKQJT4CAQ52,SK8HKJ983D8652C93|sv|e|
mb|1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I have a great hand, worth much more than its 11 HCP. 6-5 distribution and a void are wonderful. And all the HCP are in my two longest suits that is great. The hand has 11 HCP and 3 length points for 14 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|SB|S|mb|2D|AN|Natural Game Force|
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@H is natural showing 4+ hearts.|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@S shows exactly 3-card support. If North had 4-card support they must respond with Jacoby 2N rather than 2@D. The 2D bid 100% denies 4-card spade support.|
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|3@H is control bid (@HA), denying control in clubs (no A, K, singleton or void) and control in diamonds (no A or K). Note that had North not bid 2@D, then South would make a control bid of 3@D since he has a void which is 1st round control. |
PG| ***** 27 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But if partner bids a suit, your control bids in that suit only show aces or kings, not voids or singletons. Voids and singletons are not useful in partner's suit.|
PG| ***** 28 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4C|an|Ace or King|
PG| ***** 29 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|4@C control in clubs (@CA) and, since South denied a diamond control, also a control in diamonds (@DK). If North did not have both clubs or diamonds controlled, since South denied controls in those 2 suits, North would simply bid 4@S. |
PG| ***** 30 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In that case, she knows that slam is not possible if she is missing a control in either minor suit because we must have two losers in the suit in which she lacks a control.|
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|4@H repeated control bid in hearts, showing the first round control in hearts (usually @HA, rarely a void). If you repeat a control bid, it shows first round control.|
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4N|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|4N is RKCB for spades.|
PG| ***** 33 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|5H|an|2 keys no SQ|
PG| ***** 34 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|5@H is 2 key cards (@HA and @SA) and denies the @SQ.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|5S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|You should only bid slam if your side has all 5 key cards or 4 key cards and the Queen. Since NS have only 3 key cards between them and lack the @SQ, slam is not possible. In fact, it now turns out that 5@S might be going down if NS end up losing to the two missing key cards and the @SQ.|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 37 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|C6|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is not clear how to play this hand. One easy way is to take the diamond ruffing finesse, and if it works draw one round of trump and concede 2 spade tricks. Another is to take the heart finesse and set up hearts. I like the diamond finesse best.|
PG| ***** 38 ***** |


