mb|1N|mb|P|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With a weak hand and 5-4 in the majors, you should always transfer and not bid |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| because Stayman promises at least an invitational hand.|
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Here if I bid 2@C and partner bids 2@D and I bid 2@H that shows an invitational hand with 5 hearts and 4 spades. There is a convention called |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?ndf=crawlingstayman,Crawling Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| where that sequence would ask partner to pass with better hearts or correct to 2@S with better spades. But that is not standard.|
PG| ***** 72 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So we will play standard and I bid 2@D which is a transfer and partner needs to bid 2@H and I pass letting the stranger hand play.|
PG| ***** 73 ***** |


